, "ALDOB:ALDOB is a gene located on chromosome 9q22.3 that encodes the enzyme fructose-1,6-bisphosphate aldolase. This enzyme plays a crucial role in fructose metabolism. Additionally, ALDOB is significant in the context of hereditary fructose intolerance, as it is the gene responsible for encoding the enzyme that is deficient in this condition.", "DÉFICIT PERIFÉRICO:Déficit periférico is a clinical form of galactosemia limited to erythrocytes and leukocytes, resulting in asymptomatic individuals.", "DÉFICIT GENERALIZADO:Déficit generalizado is a clinical form of galactosemia where GALE activity is deficient in all tissues, resembling classic galactosemia.", "DÉFICIT INTERMEDIO:Déficit intermedio is a clinical form of galactosemia with reduced GALE activity in erythrocytes and leukocytes, but not presenting acute symptoms at birth.", "FRUCTOSA-1-FOSFATO:Fructose-1-phosphate is a compound that accumulates in the body due to the deficiency of the enzyme fructose-1,6-bisphosphate aldolase.", "FRUCTOSA-6-FOSFATO:Fructose-6-phosphate is an intermediate in the glycolytic pathway that is affected by fructose metabolism.", "FRUCTOSA-1,6 BIFOSFATO:Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate is a key intermediate in the glycolytic pathway that is produced from fructose-1-phosphate.", "GLICERALDEHIDO:Glyceraldehyde is a product of fructose metabolism that is involved in energy production.", "GLICERALDEHIDO-3-FOSFATO:Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is an important intermediate in the glycolytic pathway derived from glyceraldehyde.", "DIHIDROXIACETONA FOSFATO:Dihydroxyacetone phosphate is another product of fructose metabolism that plays a role in energy production.", "MUSCULO Y OTROS TEJIDOS:Muscle and other tissues are involved in the metabolism of fructose and its intermediates.", "HEREDITARY FRUCTOSE INTOLERANCE:Hereditary fructose intolerance is a genetic condition that impairs the body's ability to metabolize fructose. This metabolic disorder can lead to a range of clinical manifestations, particularly complicating dietary management in infants. Individuals with this condition are unable to properly process fructose, which can result in various health issues."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}